  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Kevzara (sarilumab), an IL-6 receptor antagonist. Version 1; Original: 03/13/2023; Accepted: 4/21/2023; Effective: 6/1/2023.",
    "Closed indication selection attests to the FDA diagnosis and treatment-response qualifiers. Both indications require adults and rheumatology prescribing or consultation. PMR diagnosis must be consistent with EULAR/ACR criteria; explicit consistency attestation is encoded without a separate criteria checklist. PMR approval #4 OR #5 is encoded as either qualifying steroid-history path.",
    "Initial authorization must include previous therapies trialed and the nature of the failure. Patients established on manufacturer-supplied samples or manufacturer-sponsored assistance must still meet initial authorization criteria as patients new to therapy.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 6 months. RA requires documented positive clinical response in at least one objective measure (e.g. CDAI, SDAI, PAS). PMR requires improved adherence to corticosteroid taper and a decreased number of flares while on Kevzara.",
    "Quantity limit (notes only): 200 mg (1.14 ml) subcutaneously once every 14 days. Quantity enforcement requires manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): increased risk of serious infections, including opportunistic infections, which may lead to hospitalization or death; many affected patients were receiving concomitant immunosuppressants. Evaluate tuberculosis, HIV, hepatitis B and hepatitis C before treatment. Live vaccines should generally not be administered during treatment unless the benefit outweighs the risk.",
    "PDL status unknown: source is silent. Infliximab is linked for RA overlap and requires its own indication-specific review; it is not a PMR alternative.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation of prior therapies and nature of failure, authorization duration, reauthorization response documentation, dosing, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
